menu "Yaykit board"

config YK_BOARD_LCD_BUFFER_LINES
    int "LVGL draw buffer height (lines)"
    range 8 466
    default 40
    help
        One band of this many lines (466 x lines x 2 bytes) in internal, DMA-capable RAM. 40 lines (37 KB) by
        default; the Yay main firmware, which also runs Wi-Fi, TLS and the speech models, uses fewer to keep
        40 KB of internal RAM free. Keep it even (the panel's even-start rule).

config YK_BOARD_LVGL_CORE
    int "Core for the LVGL task (-1: either)"
    range -1 1
    default -1
    help
        The Yay main firmware pins it to core 0: its audio front end takes over half of core 1 while listening, and
        the frame that shows 「我在听」 must not wait behind it.

config YK_BOARD_TOUCH_INT_GPIO
    int "Touch controller interrupt pin (-1: polled)"
    range -1 48
    default -1
    help
        TP_INT of the CST820. The reference schematic puts it on GPIO11 or GPIO13. Measured 2026-10-21: GPIO13
        toggles at 59 Hz (the panel's TE), GPIO11 idles high, so TP_INT should be GPIO11; set it once a touch
        confirms it. Until then the fast touch reader polls (board_touch_fast_start).

endmenu
